{
  "name": "OldSettingRowStillReads",
  "comment": "A settings row saved before this stage still reads (ruling 7, decision 774). A saved\nrow is read into its class by its key (`<actor>!<path>`), which already says which\nclass — the row's own `kind` field is no longer the class picker. A row saved in\ntoday's shape ({setting, kind: <path>}) reads back after the change. Guard — green\ntoday (today's binary saves and reads today's shape); must stay green after. Settings\nrun in-memory under `--test` (setting-<app.id>, per PLang/app/actor/setting/this.cs),\nso save+read in one run proves the round-trip; a committed sqlite fixture couldn't be\nloaded in test mode (`Mode.Test` forces in-memory). The cross-binary read is proved by\nthe suite surviving the stage 2 change, not by this test alone.",
  "step": [
